 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It's mildly controversial. Some people do it and never get caught. Then it's worth checking with your local authority first. They usually don't mind if you ask first and ask for permission. Generally only on Saturday and Sunday, and only with small packed sandwiches and drinks. You need permission and a Permissive Use notice in view at every spot. Keep it down and turn off cars arriving. Most people wouldn't mind a bit of singing together if you asked first. If you do get permission, ask about other landmarks and other graves you might run into. Some area have specific guidelines.",
